< func (c *Client) Close() error
<     Close releases the client's network resources: it closes the idle
<     connections of the transport the client built or cloned (WithHTTPTransport),
<     and calls Close once on a WithRoundTripper transport that implements
<     io.Closer, returning its error. Calls in flight finish on their own
<     connections. Close is idempotent: a second Close does nothing and returns
<     nil. Every call made after Close fails with a *ConfigError wrapping
<     ErrClientClosed.
